<title>ITALY: Italian charter cargo flights mainly for Alitalia.</title>
<headline>Italian charter cargo flights mainly for Alitalia.</headline>
<dateline>ROME 1997-06-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Movements of cargo charter flights into and out of Italian airports last year was dominated by foreign airlines flying on behalf of Alitalia, statistics issued by the ministry of transport civil aviation department (Civilavia) show.</p>
<p>A total of 1,706 cargo charter flights were operated in and out of Italy last year against 1,730 in 1995 when figures were swollen by small planes flying between Catania in Sicily and Malta.</p>
<p>No Italian airline was listed amongst the 57 that operated cargo charters to and from Italy last year. But 682 flights - 292 outgoing and 390 incoming - or 40 percent of the total were operated on behalf of Alitalia.</p>
<p>The main markets were the north America with 663 flights for a market share of nearly 39 percent and the former Soviet Union with 535 flights for a 31 percent market share.</p>
